  "scope": "Fixed16 TRAIN batches, M95 eval forward. Instance feature centroids are means of the final encoder inst_feats over each instance's superpoints (native sp_ins_labels), centred on the scene mean because deep features share a dominant mean direction that inflates raw cosine. For each recoverable failure we rank every instance by cosine similarity to the instance the deployed query actually segmented; best_target_rank is the rank of the referred instance in that ranking, so rank 1 means the encoder features make the referred instance the nearest neighbour of the wrongly selected one. Self-similarity is excluded. Also reported: pairwise similarity null over all instance pairs in the scene, and the spatial distance between the two centroids. Under the null (no instance-specific content) the target rank would be uniform over the instances, i.e. about half the scene. Diagnosis only; no model, novelty or efficacy admission.",
